To model America/Vancouver as permanent DST in order for formatting APIs to show
Pacific Daylight Time instead of Pacific Standard Time (which is wrong), Mountain
Standard Time (technically right, confusing), or GMT-7 (even more technically
right, but is also confusing).
A distant future transition is needed to workaround a ZoneInfoData
(actual implementation of java.util.TimeZone) bug. Its abbreviation is PacT:
  * PDT can't be used as otherwise zic will drop it as it's identical to the
    previous transition.
  * Abbreviations are used in libc APIs only and for timestamps too far in the
    future.
  * All other APIs are backed by CLDR data and timestamps after 9 Mar 2026 will be
    formatted as 'Pacific Daylight Time'.

